    "narrative": "Ghost Ride the WHIP enters today\u2019s slate with a clear emphasis on aggressive base-stealing opportunities and favorable park factors. Our highest-rated play is **James Wood** (78.42), who benefits from a leaky matchup against Chandler and a high-volume stolen base environment; his elite xwOBA of 0.420 makes him an essential anchor in the outfield. Close behind are **Mickey Moniak** (75.75) and **Brice Turang** (73.40). **Mickey Moniak** is effectively weaponizing a strong park adjustment and a platoon edge against Mahle, while **Brice Turang**\u2019s leadoff status against E-Rod, combined with the high SB-success rate against the pitcher, makes him a primary engine for our category targets. **Seiya Suzuki** (67.40) and **Josh Naylor** (70.02) round out a balanced offensive core, with both players drawing significant efficiency boosts from the opposing starter's mediocre xERA and favorable lineup placement.\n\nThe most difficult roster decision today was keeping **Cole Young** on the bench at 49.98. He narrowly missed the cut behind **Alex Freeland** (55.54), whose projection surged due to a high-upside matchup against the vulnerable Sears. While **Cole Young** offers stability, the optimizer favored the sheer efficiency of **Alex Freeland**\u2019s specific platoon advantage. We are also keeping a close watch on **Gabriel Moreno** (59.17) and **Max Muncy** (53.64); while **Gabriel Moreno** benefits from the #4 spot, his matchup against Sproat remains the tightest margin in our lineup. Risks are currently minimal, though owners should monitor the wind in parks hosting **Kyle Karros** and **Mickey Moniak**, as the +14% park boost is a significant driver of their elevated scores today. We remain committed to maximizing our stolen base potential across the board, ensuring that even our marginal starters provide utility in the scarcity categories.",
